el for this concept. A single string, a single language-tagged value, or an array of language-tagged values. Each language should appear at most once.","required":true,"sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.skosProperties.skosConcept"],"effectiveId":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel"},{"path":["cdif:hasPhysicalMapping","cdif:physicalDataType","_anyOf","1","schema:termCode"],"id":"http://schema.org/termCode","description":"A representative code for this keyword in the controlled vocabulary. Analogous to skos:Notation","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.definedTerm"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/termCode"},{"path":["cdif:hasPhysicalMapping","cdif:physicalDataType","_anyOf","1","schema:inDefinedTermSet"],"id":"http://schema.org/inDefinedTermSet","description":"The controlled vocabulary responsible for this keyword, as EITHER a plain URI string identifying the vocabulary, OR an object reference ({\"@id\": \"<uri>\"}) to a vocabulary defined elsewhere in the document. Both forms are already in use across CDIF profiles and downstream ADA building blocks; permitting only the string form made the object form - the natural JSON-LD spelling of a reference - invalid, while this class's own union-type policy above explicitly anticipates both.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.definedTerm"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/inDefinedTermSet"},{"path":["cdif:hasPhysicalMapping","cdif:physicalDataType","_anyOf","1","schema:identifier"],"id":"http://schema.org/identifier","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.definedTerm"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/identifier"},{"path":["cdif:hasPhysicalMapping","cdif:physicalDataType","_anyOf","1","schema:identifier","schema:propertyID"],"id":"http://schema.org/propertyID","description":"In this context for the schema:PropertyValue, this field is an identifier for the identifier schema, e.g. DOI, ARK.  Get values from https://registry.identifiers.org/registry/ for interoperability. URI-shape values MUST be serialized as JSON-LD IRI references ({\"@id\":\"...\"}) so they participate in RDF entailment; free-label strings remain valid as strings.","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.identifier"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/propertyID"},{"path":["cdif:hasPhysicalMapping","cdif:physicalDataType","_anyOf","1","schema:identifier","schema:value"],"id":"http://schema.org/value","description":"the identifier string. E.g. 10.5066/F7VX0DMQ","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.identifier"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/value"},{"path":["cdif:hasPhysicalMapping","cdif:physicalDataType","_anyOf","1","schema:identifier","schema:url"],"id":"http://schema.org/url","description":"web-resolveable string for the identifier; host name part is location of a resolver that will return some representation for the given identifier value. E.g. https://doi.org/10.5066/F7VX0DMQ ","schema_type":"string","format":"uri","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.identifier"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/url"},{"path":["cdif:hasPhysicalMapping","cdif:physicalDataType","_anyOf","1","schema:name"],"id":"http://schema.org/name","description":"text label for the term that is useful to human user","schema_type":"string","sources":["bblocks://cdif.bbr.metadata.schemaorgProperties.definedTerm"],"effectiveId":"http://schema.org/name"}]}